# `lib/`

Project-local libraries live here. Each subdirectory is treated as an independent library that PlatformIO discovers automatically.

## What belongs here

- Third-party libraries that are intentionally vendored because they need project-specific patches.
- Small helper libraries that do not belong in the public registry and are only used by this project.

## Currently vendored libraries

| Library | Why it is vendored |
| --- | --- |
| `lib/CAN` | Patched MCP2515 CAN library with 20 MHz crystal support. The upstream `sandeepmistry/arduino-CAN` does not include the required CNF table for 20 MHz crystals, so this project maintains a local patched copy. Do not replace this with a registry dependency without verifying crystal-frequency support. |

## Adding or updating libraries

1. Copy the library into a new subdirectory, for example `lib/NewLibrary`.
2. Apply any necessary patches and document them in a `README.md` or comments at the top of patched files.
3. Ensure `platformio.ini` does **not** include a conflicting `lib_deps` entry for the same library name; PlatformIO prefers the local copy automatically.
4. Update this README to explain the vendoring rationale.

## Do not assume unpatched upstream

For `lib/CAN`, assume the patched behavior is required for 20 MHz MCP2515 boards. If you need a different crystal frequency, check the MCP2515 CNF configuration in `lib/CAN/src/MCP2515.cpp` before changing the library or adding an alternative dependency.

## PlatformIO details

PlatformIO's Library Dependency Finder (LDF) scans `lib/` automatically. For more details on how dependencies are resolved, see the [PlatformIO LDF documentation](https://docs.platformio.org/page/librarymanager/ldf.html).

